course: dictionary
lesson: 6010
title: The median: the middle one
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: In maths, the median is the middle number when a list of numbers is put in order from smallest to largest. First sort the numbers, then find the one in the middle.
explain: Think of children lined up by height, shortest to tallest. The child standing in the middle is the median height. Half the line is shorter and half is taller.
explain: The word also appears in the news. «The median age splits the people in half, half younger and half older.» So the median age is the age where exactly half the people are younger and half are older. Check the meaning by swapping in your own words: «the middle one when they are in order» still makes sense.
explain: Median has other meanings too. On a road, the median (US: median strip) is the strip of land between the two sides. In geometry, a median is a line from a corner of a triangle to the middle of the opposite side. Use the sentence around the word to tell which meaning is meant.
fact: The median is the middle number when a list of numbers is in order.
fact: You must put the numbers in order first, or you will not find the middle.
fact: «The median age splits the people in half, half younger and half older.»
fact: «In Niger the median age is under 16, and in Japan it is about 49.»
fact: In the UK and Australia, the median is the strip of land between the two sides of a road; in the US it is called the median strip.
exercise: Put these numbers in order: 2, 9, 5, 7, 4. What is the median? | 9 | 7 | 4 | *5
exercise: «The median age splits the people in half.» What does median mean here? | A number that is always zero | The youngest person in the group | The oldest person in the group | *The middle point, with half older and half younger
exercise: On a road, what is the median? | *The strip of land between the two sides of a road | A type of car | The line where cars must stop | The edge of the pavement
test: Which number is the median of 3, 8, 1, 6, 10? | *6 | 1 | 3 | 10
test: In geometry, what is a median? | A line that is the same length as each side | A line that goes all the way round the triangle | *A line from a corner of a triangle to the middle of the opposite side | A curved edge of a shape
exam: The ages of five children are 8, 10, 9, 12 and 11. What is the median age? | 9 | 12 | *10 | 8
